+\begin{statement}{E.17}{Proved}{Independent pentagon checks on the published small targets}
+For the three published targets $\mathcal N^{(0)}$,
+$\mathcal N^{(1)}$, $\mathcal N^{(2)}$ in
+\citet[Table~1]{DolgushevLeLorenz2024}, the independently
+recomputed results are
+\[
+\begin{array}{c|r|r|r|r|r}
+ i&|PB_4/\mathcal N^{(i)}|&|B_3/\mathcal N^{(i)}_3|&
+ n&\text{practical}&\text{charming}\\\hline
+0&8&192&4&4&4\\1&8&192&4&8&4\\2&12&648&3&18&6.
+\end{array}
+\]
+Every charming shadow in the first two rows is genuine.
+These two targets have the same induced arity-three kernel,
+but their practical-shadow sets differ.
+\end{statement}
+\begin{proof}
+The six permutation generators for each target were obtained
+from the authors' data file \texttt{subGrPB4\_org35} in their
+PackageGT archive \citep{Dolgushev2022PackageGT}.
+The independent script \texttt{e\_dll\_pentagons.py} checks the
+pure braid presentation, verifies preservation of its kernel
+under all three braid conjugations on every finite Cayley edge,
+and constructs the five insertion/cabling maps. Their diagonal
+image identifies the arity-three kernel exactly with kernel
+$315$ of the completed table in the first two rows and kernel
+$1203$ in the third row.
+
+For every friendly $m$ and every $f\in H$, the program checks
+both hexagons, surjectivity, and the actual pentagon in the
+published $PB_4$ quotient. Restricting to $H'$ gives exactly
+the charming counts displayed. In the first two rows $H$ has
+class two and the computation of E.16 gives all four genuine
+pairs; alternatively, four distinct friendly $m$ residues and
+cyclotomic surjectivity already force this conclusion.
+The third row has a certified genuine sublist containing
+identity and complex conjugation; genuineness of its other
+four charming shadows is not inferred from its finite equations.
+
+The first two rows also show why the refinement convention
+matters. They have $|X|=|C|=4$ and pure abelianization of order
+$16$, whereas unchanged linking kernel would require $4^3=64$.
+Their canonical E.15 refinement has braid quotient order $768$,
+not $192$. Thus an actual small arity-four target need not be
+the forgetful target constructed from its own induced
+arity-three quotient.
+\end{proof}
